ly phonetic sets with more than two characters are displayed.</p><p>There is still one other variable that comes to mind regarding these phonetic sets. That is the trustworthyness of the component to provide the phonetic information. The phonetic sets displayed only show characters where the component "works". What about the characters where the component failed to provide the same information? The academic term for this is called combinality. HanziCraft is working on trying to provide this information as well.</p><div class="printable-cta"><a href="https://gum.co/IQaoa" target="_blank"><h4>Get the new printout for $5</h4></a><a href="https://gum.co/IQaoa" target="_blank"><img src="https://hanzicraft.com/printableart.jpg"></a></div><h4>Regularity Degree One (exact same pronunciation including tone)</h4><ol style="padding: 0px;"><li class="list"><div class="list_head">å­zi3: 
